  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the skewness of the lotteries by comparing how probabilities are distributed across favorable and unfavorable outcomes, and preferring the more right-skewed one (here, A). The individual, however, focuses only on the magnitude of the loss in B ('Wert ist allerdings bei B höher') and acknowledges both have high loss chances, but does not compare the relative concentration of probability on worse outcomes or reference distributional shape. There is no indication that the individual assessed which lottery has a greater probability mass on unfavorable outcomes relative to favorable ones, nor that they preferred the more right-skewed option. The justification is outcome-centered (how bad is the loss if it happens) rather than distribution-centered (how likely are worse outcomes). Therefore, the information considered and the reasoning rule applied by the individual do not align with the decision reason. It is unlikely the individual used skewness as a basis for choice.",
